186045417 true] [17592186420182 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420182 1083 #uuid "ef0b3c15-c486-552b-8364-93f50ed30f9a" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420173 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420183 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420183 1077 "field-1" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420183 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420173 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420183 1079 #uuid "49fca85c-c10d-570a-9fbd-829efc317583" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420183 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1069 "q-341252" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1071 "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is the value of $f(-3)?$\n\n$f(-3)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1072 #uuid "75e9cee8-821a-5456-9b71-a9061b7a8387" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true] [17592186420184 1074 "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the even extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =F(-x) \\\\  & =(-x)^{2}{e}^{(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{2}{e}^{(-3)^{2}}=9{e}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534358 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-03ab0d3f-c0ec-5341-aee5-a68517e3ea54" 17592186420172 "answer-15bb385e-7f13-50d3-937e-b59ebadbf90b" 17592186420173 "answer-3ef189ae-b8a9-5aad-a7b1-aabed08f2956" 17592186420174 "answer-40d92551-833d-5ca4-a56b-7ab1b74f7b82" 17592186420175 "answer-5ccfdcc9-57